    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0291" n="279" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg279"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">875.01/9–2844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Alexander C. Kirk, Political Adviser, Allied Force
                        Headquarters, to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caserta</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-28T14:00:00+01:00">September 28,
                            1944—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:07 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>575. Reference my 451, September 19.<anchor n="33" xml:id="d199-f1"/> BAF Policy
                    Committee is being asked to consider desirability of extending aid to LNC beyond
                    time of German withdrawal from Albania on grounds its political opponents will
                    inherit surplus German arms. This is frankly recognized as direct intervention
                    in Albania’s internal affairs and seems unnecessary since most Allied sources in
                    Bari now believe that civil war can be avoided except possibly in a few areas in
                    northeast and Kossovo. As reported in our No. 572, September 28,<anchor n="34"
                        xml:id="d199-f2"/> the recent disunity and distintegration among Nationalist
                    elements and desertions to LNC make it unlikely that German arms could be used
                    effectively even if left behind in anti-LNC hands. Moreover, it is assumed some
                    Allied occupational troops will arrive in time.</p>
                <pb facs="0292" n="280" xml:id="pg280"/>
                <p>In addition, LNC has lately given indication of a softening attitude towards its
                    political opponents, Kupi excluded.</p>
                <p>The Department’s comments would be appreciated as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
